# Pairs with RAllOrNothing. The base's transport may drop a delivery and
# deliver a record again, but never loses one: a record leaves the outbox only
# once it has been applied. This mutation lets a prepare be acknowledged
# without being applied - what the receiver's dead-letter applier does today
# after its retries run out (issue #4591), and what a trim of an unread entry
# did at the sender before #4577 made the shipper withhold a peer's saga
# records across a TTL gap (issue #4534) and #4595 gave it an offset floor
# (issue #4579). The shipper's terminal hold counts
# the acknowledged prepare as delivered and releases the saga's terminals; the
# tally completes, the other key's bucket drains post-saga, and the lost key has
# no bucket and stays pre-saga. Once the decision is recorded a later copy of
# the prepare would be settled, so the split shows when nothing re-ships it.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingPrepareAckedUnapplied
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a prepare is acknowledged without being applied, so its saga's terminals are released over a key with no bucket
PERTURBS: DeliverPrepare

--- FIND
    /\ \/ outbox' = outbox \ {m}
       \/ outbox' = outbox
    /\ rpend' = IF SettleView(m.key) = "inflight" /\ rterm[m.key] = "none"
                THEN [rpend EXCEPT ![m.key] = "pending"] ELSE rpend
    /\ rproj' = IF SettleView(m.key) = "committed" THEN [rproj EXCEPT ![m.key] = "post"] ELSE rproj
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a delivery may be acknowledged without being applied.
    /\ \/ /\ \/ outbox' = outbox \ {m}
             \/ outbox' = outbox
          /\ rpend' = IF SettleView(m.key) = "inflight" /\ rterm[m.key] = "none"
                      THEN [rpend EXCEPT ![m.key] = "pending"] ELSE rpend
          /\ rproj' = IF SettleView(m.key) = "committed" THEN [rproj EXCEPT ![m.key] = "post"] ELSE rproj
       \/ /\ outbox' = outbox \ {m}
          /\ UNCHANGED <<rpend, rproj>>
--- END
